      "message": "[warning] Line 57: 🟡 When a local reaction is pending removal, `toggle` can immediately re-add the same emoji instead of waiting for removal completion. This happens because `ownReactions` filters out pending removals, so a second tap before backend confirmation falls into `add(...)`. That contradicts the intended \"skip removal already sent until gone\" behavior and can create remove/add races with non-deterministic end state. Keep pending removals visible to `toggle` (or explicitly short-circuit when the tapped emoji has a pending removal for this message) so repeated taps are ignored until `reactionsUpdated` clears the pending entry.",
